{
  "meta": {
    "templateCredsSetupCompleted": false
  },
  "name": "Score weekly Sales Navigator leads with AI and sync them to HubSpot",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "17d9f90b-e4d0-4c3b-93f7-4915a231dcbd",
      "name": "Template overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -720,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## Score weekly Sales Navigator leads with AI and sync them to HubSpot\n\n**Who it's for:** sales and growth teams that prospect in LinkedIn Sales Navigator and run their pipeline in HubSpot.\n\n**What it does:** every Monday, Evaboot exports your saved Sales Navigator search and finds verified emails. Each lead with a deliverable email is scored against your ideal customer profile by an AI model, which also writes a one-line icebreaker. Leads at or above your score threshold are created or updated in HubSpot with their score and icebreaker. A Slack message reports how many leads were exported, deliverable and pushed.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Install the Evaboot community node (`@evaboot-team/n8n-nodes-evaboot`). **Self-hosted n8n only.**\n2. Add credentials: Evaboot API key (Evaboot dashboard > API), OpenAI, HubSpot app token, Slack.\n3. In HubSpot, create two contact properties: `evaboot_icp_score` (number) and `evaboot_icebreaker` (single-line text).\n4. Fill in **Set your search and ICP**: Sales Navigator URL, ICP description, minimum score, Slack channel.\n5. Activate the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\nEvaboot account with Sales Navigator connected, OpenAI API key, HubSpot, Slack.\n\n### How to customize\nChange the schedule, rewrite the ICP prompt, raise the score threshold, or swap HubSpot for another CRM node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7b9df0eb-2d47-4960-8c2a-07e050ee8643",
      "name": "Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -160,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 460,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "### 1. Configure and export\nEvery Monday the workflow reads your settings and asks Evaboot to export the Sales Navigator search. Evaboot scrapes the leads and finds and verifies their emails."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "da94d0f6-d247-4c37-89b8-7c072af0a332",
      "name": "Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        340,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 700,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "### 2. Wait for the export\nThe workflow checks the export every 5 minutes. Only the export started by this run is read, so manual exports on your Evaboot account are never pushed. A 2,500-lead export with emails takes about an hour."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f4575944-ee55-4d86-965f-8cce8131d83c",
      "name": "Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1080,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "### 3. Score each lead with AI\nLeads without a deliverable email are dropped. The AI model compares each remaining lead to your ICP and returns a 0-100 score, a one-sentence reason and an icebreaker. Leads below your minimum score stop here."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2faa5745-6bec-491c-a55b-1ae50d116756",
      "name": "Step 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2160,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 700,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "### 4. Sync to HubSpot and report\nQualified leads are created or updated in HubSpot (matched on email) with their score and icebreaker. Slack then gets a one-line summary of the run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e65facc0-e72b-4741-82a9-0db0bdb1d05d",
      "name": "Every Monday at 8am",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        -100,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "weeks",
              "triggerAtDay": [
                1
              ],
              "triggerAtHour": 8
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b61f0df2-8dc5-4ee5-9e77-e280046c57e9",
      "name": "Set your search and ICP",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        100,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "9e9e629e-271b-44a3-8410-9d554a574e5d",
              "name": "salesNavigatorUrl",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "https://www.linkedin.com/sales/search/people?query=REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_SEARCH"
            },
            {
              "id": "49460077-46d2-4081-956c-aaaff1896d03",
              "name": "idealCustomerProfile",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "B2B SaaS companies with 50 to 500 employees. Decision makers in sales, revenue operations or growth (Head of, Director, VP, C-level)."
            },
            {
              "id": "a32f1718-5751-4819-8280-571f11330650",
              "name": "minimumScore",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 70
            },
            {
              "id": "e7009d7a-4f93-4820-826d-e1271dc3d331",
              "name": "slackChannel",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "#sales-leads"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
